+        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.5-1">Management protocols are required to support on-line interactions between PKI user and management entities.  For example, a management protocol might be used between a CA and a client system with which a key pair is associated, or between two CAs which cross-certify each other.  The set of functions which potentially need to be supported by management protocols include:</t>
